WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:08.390
No Google account? No problem. Here's how to sign in with your volunteer code. Your phone remembers you after that.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:19.150
Step one. Type your volunteer code, and tap Open my page. Your code is in any email from the Hub. Dashes and capital letters don't matter.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:26.520
Step two. You're in! This phone or computer remembers you, so next time, just open the page.

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:33.440
Step three. Don't have your code? Tap, Email it to me. It's right under Open my page.

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:39.304
Step four. Enter the email your Hub emails come to, and tap Email my code.

00:00:39.504 --> 00:00:44.230
Family on one email? Everyone's code comes in the same email.

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:51.630
Step five. In the email, tap Open my volunteer page. It signs you in on that phone or computer.

00:00:51.830 --> 00:00:55.870
Your code is in the email too, for your other devices.

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:09.270
Step six. To switch between family members, tap a name at the top. A dotted name with a plus shares your email. Tap it to add them to this device. Plus Add, signs in someone else.

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:18.020
Step seven. On a shared computer? When you're done, tap Forget me on this device, so the next person can't open your page.

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:24.503
One more tip. Typing your email instead of your code shows your shifts, hours, and paperwork.

00:01:24.703 --> 00:01:30.810
Your code opens everything, including your paperwork page, and naming your extra spots.

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:36.600
Questions? Email the IU liaison from the bottom of any Hub page.
